From a6bdc7894d4f7e2dc9ad4e6d731f279cea7b571c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:04:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/31] [PD] dcp: Relayout a DCP-sharded DSA draft KV like the
 target

On ROCm the DSA MTP draft stripes its KV like the DCP target, but the
DCP1 -> DCP-N relayout assumed a replicated draft and raised in the
draft head-slicing path. The prefill now applies the decode's draft
sharding rule and sends the draft with the target's rows and pack.
NIXL and Mori reject a sharded draft until ported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
